WEBVTT

00:01.200 --> 00:05.100
Spaceadom turns your spacebar into an app launcher.

00:05.200 --> 00:09.700
Here is everything it can do, one feature at a time.

00:12.000 --> 00:16.100
Hold Space and tap a letter. The app opens.

00:16.400 --> 00:19.900
Tap the same letter again. It tucks away.

00:20.200 --> 00:23.900
Once more and it’s back. Open, tuck away, back.

00:24.200 --> 00:28.300
Hiding behind another window? One tap brings it to the front.

00:28.400 --> 00:32.500
Tap Space on its own and it types a space, like always.

00:32.400 --> 00:35.900
Fast typing stays typing. Only a held Space is a shortcut.

00:38.000 --> 00:41.900
Hold Space for a beat and every shortcut appears around it.

00:41.800 --> 00:45.700
Your apps, and the Spaceadom specials in their own colour.

00:45.600 --> 00:49.700
Let go without a letter and nothing happens.

00:52.000 --> 00:55.900
Space + Esc is the boss key: every window hides, the sound mutes.

00:56.200 --> 00:59.100
Press it again and everything comes back.

00:59.200 --> 01:02.900
Space + ` puts the window in a corner and keeps it on top.

01:05.000 --> 01:09.100
One key can hold a group of apps, up to six.

01:09.400 --> 01:12.700
Same rhythm. They open together, tuck away together…

01:12.800 --> 01:15.700
…and come back together, side by side or in a grid.

01:15.800 --> 01:19.900
Make a group in any key’s editor and pick the layout.

01:22.000 --> 01:25.900
Hold the mouse wheel. Your apps bloom around the cursor.

01:25.800 --> 01:29.500
Drift toward one and let go. That’s it.

01:29.600 --> 01:33.300
Prefer the Back or Forward button? Pick any of the three.

01:33.200 --> 01:36.900
CAD and 3D apps like SolidWorks keep their middle button.

01:39.000 --> 01:42.900
Slide a finger up the left edge of the touchpad for brightness.

01:43.000 --> 01:46.500
The right edge is volume.

01:46.600 --> 01:49.900
The top edge scrubs a video. The middle still moves the pointer.

01:49.800 --> 01:52.900
Brightness follows your cursor, external monitors included.

01:55.000 --> 01:58.500
Little windows: a pop-up timer…

01:58.400 --> 02:01.700
…a notepad that saves as you type…

02:01.600 --> 02:04.700
…and a round frame for one picture you love.

02:04.600 --> 02:07.100
Open them with Space and a key you choose, or from the tray.

02:08.600 --> 02:11.900
Not sure how fast you type? Press Calibrate.

02:11.800 --> 02:15.100
Type one sentence, then a few shortcuts.

02:15.000 --> 02:18.000
It sets the beat to fit your hands.

02:19.600 --> 02:23.300
Space + one key moves your sound to the next speaker.

02:23.400 --> 02:28.000
Tick the speakers and mics it cycles. The rest are skipped.

02:30.000 --> 02:33.700
Space Boost: the app you tapped flies down into its toast.

02:33.600 --> 02:37.900
It’s off by default. Turn it on in Settings, under Appearance.

02:40.000 --> 02:43.700
Profiles give the same keyboard a different set of apps.

02:43.600 --> 02:46.700
Space + Right Alt switches: work, play, study.

02:46.600 --> 02:49.900
The profile’s emoji sits on the SPACE pill, so you always know.

02:51.300 --> 02:55.300
Spaceadom is free, made by student developers. A coffee keeps it going.

02:55.400 --> 03:00.000
Free on the Microsoft Store. Windows 10 and 11, a Mac beta, and Linux coming.
